comment.body:
@clawsweeper re-review

Updated the PR head with the CI format fix (import ordering for the admission-error module); all CI gates pass on the current head.

The regression now asserts the issue's core contract directly: the typed admission error must reach the replayable transcript-commit classifier. Specifically `openclaw-agent-db-validation-cache.test.ts` asserts `isReplayableWorkerTranscriptCommitError(adoptionError) === true` for the schema-admission race, in addition to `toBeInstanceOf(AgentDatabaseSchemaAdmissionChangedError)` and the preserved message — so the retry/replay path actually classifies the typed error rather than a bare `Error` (#188935).
